      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think if you do something like\n\n```\n#define stream_renderer_error(format, ...)                                           \n    do {\n        stream_renderer_debug(STREAM_RENDERER_DEBUG_ERROR, \n                              \"[%s(%d)] \" format,\n                              __FILE__,\n                              __LINE__,\n                              ##__VA_ARGS__);\n    } while (0)\n```\n\nthen you can simplify `stream_renderer_debug()` above to \n\n```\nvoid stream_renderer_debug(uint32_t type, const char* format, ...) {\n    char buf[MAX_DEBUG_BUFFER_SIZE];\n    va_list args;\n    va_start(args, format);\n    vsnprintf(buffer, sizeof(buffer), format, args);\n    va_end(args);\n    \n    ...\n}\n```\n\nwhich just needs the single `*nprintf`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 90,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 94,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "2fbef6c698485c3e7bcf49eddaf8abcfcb315cdd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
