      "writtenOn": "2023-07-26T16:17:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can we drop `debug` from the name of the callback + struct + enums and replace it with log? The commit message mentions redirecting logging to handlers and I think logging does not have the nuisance that it is disabled in release builds while we want errors (and potentially fatal logs) to always be logged (and potentially abort). I think `STREAM_RENDERER_LOGGING_LEVEL_ERROR` is easier to parse than `STREAM_RENDERER_DEBUG_ERROR` which sounds like it contains two different levels.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 109,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 109,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "2fbef6c698485c3e7bcf49eddaf8abcfcb315cdd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d4742792_083eee7e",
