      "writtenOn": "2023-07-26T19:12:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It sort of modeled on the Vulkan debug callback.\n\n https://registry.khronos.org/vulkan/specs/1.3-extensions/man/html/vkCreateDebugReportCallbackEXT.html\n \nGenerally, I think \"VulkanDebugCallback\" or \"RutabagaDebugCallback\" sounds a bit better than \"VulkanLogCallback\" or \"RutabagLogCallback\", and plus the rutabaga side already landed, so perhaps not worth chaning.\n\nBut I did add  `STREAM_RENDERER_LOG_LEVEL\" preprocrssor to control log-levels.  I think the log levels would be subset of the debug types, assuming we get the metrics code transition to this interface as well.",
      "parentUuid": "e2921ad5_9f0d67ea",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 109,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 109,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "2fbef6c698485c3e7bcf49eddaf8abcfcb315cdd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
